[38;5;231m⏺[39m I took "go ahead" to mean option 1. I added a new [38;5;153mGET /v2/users[39m that returns [38;5;153muser_id[39m, and the existing [38;5;153m/users[39m still
  returns [38;5;153muserId[39m.

  The new handler is [38;5;153mlistUsersV2[39m in [38;5;153mroutes/users.js[39m, next to the existing ones. I called both handlers directly with a
  stub response, and each returned the right field name.

  The repo has no router or server file, so I couldn't connect [38;5;153m/v2/users[39m to a URL. Whoever wires up these handlers needs
  to add that route. There are also no tests in the repo, so I didn't add any. I haven't committed anything.

  When consumers move to v2, the iOS app and the partner export will need to switch to the new path.

